  "final_message": "I've run `git status` to inspect the repository state and will check the output once it finishes.\nI am listing the files in the project to explore the structure.\nI am searching the codebase for references to `channel`.\nI am checking test files for references to `channel`.\nI am searching for existing deprecation patterns in the codebase.\nI am checking the repository history.\nI am running the test suite to establish a baseline.\nI'll wait for the test run to finish.\nWaiting for tests to complete...\nI cannot remove the `channel` field from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md).\n\n### Rationale\n\n- **ARCH-4 Rule**:\n  > `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n- Even though `channel` is not read internally within `orders-service`, [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is a public contract consumed by downstream services in other repositories. Removing `channel` directly is a breaking contract change rather than an additive change.\n- Removing `channel` from the internal [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model would also break the construction of `OrderPlaced` in [`orderPlaced()`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) unless dummy data were supplied.\n\n### Recommended Deprecation Path\n\nTo retire `channel` in compliance with **ARCH-4**:\n1. Mark the `channel` field as `@deprecated` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L16) and [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/order.ts#L23).\n2. Coordinate with the downstream consumers (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) to migrate and verify they no longer read `channel`.\n3. Follow the cross-service schema deprecation and migration lifecycle before removing the field in a future schema version.\n",
